rs ZeroFlap (ZF) active electrical cables and ZF optical transceivers, OmniConnect memory solutions, and a suite of retimers and DSPs for optical and copper Ethernet and PCIe, as well as integrated circuits, active electrical cables, and SerDes chiplets. It also provides intellectual property (IP) solutions, including SerDes IP licensing. The company offers was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in Grand Cayman, the Cayman Islands.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William J. Brennan | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 807 people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 88%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $504K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $226K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Credo Technology Group Holding  is a large-cap technology business with a $21.7B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +94% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +13.5pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -19% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 62% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $407M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.98\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 9.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 208% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.079320738699813},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $31.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 18.0% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 27% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner ali